# Runtime data.
#
# These were bare `data/` and `memory/`, and a bare pattern matches a directory
# of that name at ANY depth. That is fine while every `data` in the tree is
# runtime state, and a landmine the moment one is not: `landing/src/data/`
# builds locally, because the file is on disk, and is missing from the clone CI
# checks out. The failure lands nowhere near the cause.
#
# Anchored to the paths that really hold runtime state. `.claude/` and
# `test-results/` are already ignored wholesale, so their copies are covered.
/data/
tests/e2e/data/
/memory/
.state/
.backups/
.browser-cookies/
checkpoints/
/journal/
pids
*.pid
*.seed
*.pid.lock

# Build output (generated by client build)
public/assets/
public/index.html
public/demo-output.html
# Copied from client/public/changelog.json at build; the source of truth is
# client/public/changelog.json (regenerated by `bun run changelog`).
public/changelog.json

# Transient report from `bun run changelog` (entries missing an EN translation)
scripts/.changelog-missing-en.json

# Electron build artifacts
electron-app/dist/
electron-app/server-dist/
electron-app/release/

# Internal/confidential docs - DO NOT COMMIT
CLAUDE.md
.planning/
COMPETITOR-*.md
FEATURE-MATRIX.md
INNOVATIVE-UX-PATTERNS.md
UX-AUDIT-REPORT.md
research/
competitor-screenshots/
backups/
tasks/
docs/*
# ENV.md is the public env-var reference (env audit 2026-07) — committable.
!docs/ENV.md
!docs/generative-ui-in-chat-research.md

